    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm seeing some weird damage on my tomato plants in the greenhouse. there are these tiny little holes appearing on the leaves, almost like they're being nibbled on, but i can't find anything crawling on them during the day. i've checked for aphids and whiteflies but haven't seen much. any idea what might be causing this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This sounds like it could be spider mites, which are extremely small and often hide during the day under leaf veins or in dust layers, making them hard to spot without close inspection. The tiny holes and stippled discoloration they leave are classic signs of their feeding on tomato cells. You can confirm this by spraying your plants with a strong stream of water in the morning; if hundreds of mites fly off with the droplets, you've likely found them.",
      "source": "target",
